    "ls|LS16_S10_U_311": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.311 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \n \nCOTTON IMPEX POLICY \n \n311.  SHRI BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंरी   \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a)  the details of the cotton export and import policy of the country along with the details \nabout the share of Indian cotton exports in the world; \n \n(b)  whether the textile/fabric/clothes/ apparel are being imported from various countries \nincluding our neighbouring countries, and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  the details of export/import of cotton yarn during each of the last three years and the \ncurrent year, country-wise; and \n \n(d)  the steps taken by the Government to improve domestic textile industries? \n     \nANSWER \n         (                       ) \nMINISTER OF TEXTILES \n(SMT. SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n \n(a)�Cotton is freely importable and exportable.  Indian cotton export has \n20% share in the world.  \n \n(b)�Yes, India imports textile, fabric and apparel from various countries \nincluding our neighboring countries. Texti le and apparel imports from \ntop three suppliers to India in 2015-16 are as under: \nValues in US$ million China Bangladesh USA \nTextiles except fabric 1,030 224 286 \nFabric 1,278 39 18 \nApparel 210 144 9 \nTotal 2,518 407 313 \n \n(c)�Details of export/import of cotton yarn during each of the last three \nyears and the current year, country-wise are at Annexure-I.   \n \n(d)�In order to improve the domestic textile industry and generate \nemployment, Government has announced a special package which  \noffers labour law r eforms, additional incentives under ATUFS, \nenhanced duty drawback coverage and relaxation of Section 80JJAA \nof Income Tax Act for garment industry.  \n \n\n \nAnnexure-I \nImport of cotton yarn (In US$ Mn.) \n����� ��������� ������������� � ���������� ��������������� ������������������ �������� �������� �������� ��������\n�� ������ ������ ������ ������ ����� 