    "ls|LS16_S10_U_346": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*346     \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 9th December, 2016/ Agrahayana 18, 1938 (SAKA) \n \n \nSBI Bonds \n \n*346.  DR. K. GOPAL:            \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the State Bank of India (SBI) proposes to raise Rs. 5,000/- crore \nthrough issuance of long term bonds in domestic and overseas market to \nfinance infrastructure and affordable housing in the current fiscal and if so, the \ndetails thereof; and  \n \n(b) whether SBI has been receiving many proposals for loans under \naffordable housing policy and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE FINANCE MINISTER \n(SHRI ARUN JAITLEY) \n \n(a) & (b):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT FOR L OK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*346 FOR 9 TH \nDECEMBER, 2016 REGARDING “SBI BONDS” TABLED BY DR. K. GOPAL, \nMEMBER OF PARLIAMENT.  \n(a) & (b):  State Bank of India (SBI) has informed that its board has approved raising \nRs.5000 crore through issuance of long term  Infrastructure bonds for seven years or \nmore during the current fiscal. \n \nSBI informed that they have received and sanctioned loans under the \naffordable housing loan scheme, the details of which are as under, for the period \n01.04.16 to 31.10.16.  \nHome loan applications \nreceived (Nos.) \nAmount in crore Home  Loan Sanctioned \n(Nos.) \nAmount in crore \n143608 25811 118242 20468 \n \n******* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_347": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE PRODUCTION \nLOK  SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.347 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 9TH DECEMBER, 2016 \n \n \nMODERNIZATION OF ORDNANCE FACTORIES \n \n*347. SHRI  P. KUMAR: \n  \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE   j{kk ea=h \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of Ordnance Factories in the country along with their turnover during \nthe last two years and the current year, year-wise; \n \n(b)  whether the Government proposes to modernize certain ordnance factories and if \nso, the details thereof along with its estimated cost; and \n \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to export weapons and other equipment \nmanufactured in ordnance factories and if so, the details thereof, country-wise? \n \n   A    N    S    W    E    R \n \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                   (SHRI MANOHAR PARRIKAR) \n      j{kk ea=h              ¼Jh euksgj ijhZdj½ \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n****** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (c) OF LOK SABH A \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 347 FOR  9.12.2016   \n \n \n(a) The details of Ordnance Factories in the country along with their year -\nwise turnover during the last two years and the current year are at Annexure -I.  \n(b) Yes, Madam. Government is undertaking modernization of  Ordnance \nFactories which includes investment in Plant & Machinery and Civil Works. \nModernization of OFs is under following three major categories:  \n· Renewal & Replacement (RR) : For replacement /reconditioning of \noutlived P&M to sustain the original capacity. \n· New Capital (NC) : Acquisition of modern technology/manufacturing \nprocesses for capacity augmentation of existing product mix or \ncreation of capacity for new product. \n· Civil Infrastructure: Civil Infrastructure and services viz. Production \n& Services of buildings, Power supply, Water supply, Compressed Air \nsupply etc. \n \nSome of the major proposals include:- \n \ni. Flexible Manufacturing System[FMS] (Rs. 133 Crore) at Engine Factory \nAvadi (EFA) – for augmentation of capacity of Engines for ‘A’ vehicle \nii. Electric Arc Furnace with Ladle Furnace and Vacuum Degassing[LFVD] \n(Rs. 47 Crore) at Field Gun Factory, Kanpur ( FGK) – for modernization \nof metallurgical facilities \niii. Forging Press 3000 Ton (Rs. 122 Crore) at Field Gun Factory, Kanpur \n(FGK) – for augmentatio n of capacity of Large Caliber Barrels and \nOrdnance \niv. Electro Slag Refining [ESR] Plant (Rs. 57 Crore) at Metal & Steel \nFactory (MSF) – for augmentation of capacity of Ingots for Pinaka Motor \nTube and Large Caliber Barrels \nv. Sintering Furnace (Rs. 25 Crore) at  Heavy Alloy Penetrator Project \n(HAPP) – for augmentation of capacity of Tungsten Carbide Balls for \nPinaka Warhead  \nvi. Automatic Detonator Filling Plant (Rs. 11 Crore) at Ammunition Factory, \nKhadki ( AFK) – for modernization of facility for production of \nDetonators \n \n    Proposed investment in the ordnance factories for Financial Year 2016 -17 \nis Rs. 1461.42 Crore (RE). \n ……2/- \n\n:  2  : \n \n \n(c)  Export of arms, ammunition and weapon systems by Ordnance Factory \nBoard (OFB) is being done in accordance with broad guidelines laid for export \nto foreign countries using spare capacity after meeting the Services ’ \nrequirements and compliance to country -specific instructions issued by Ministry \nof External Affairs (MEA) from time to time. \n \nThe details of exports of weapons and other equipment planned for 2016 -\n2017 country-wise are as under: \n \nYear Country Nature of Items Value of \nOrder (USD) \nValue of \nExport(INR) \n2016-17 \n(Planned) \nIndonesia General Stores & \nClothing \n2,36,700 Exported  \nRs. 8.38 \nCrore \n(upto Nov’16) Mauritius Medium caliber \nweapon \n10,45,742 \nMaldives Small Caliber \nAmmunition \n1,10,250 \nUzbekistan General Stores & \nClothing \n3,785 \n Germany Small Caliber \nAmmunition \n8,800 \nKenya Large Caliber \nAmmunition & \nSignaling Smoke  \n10,45,048 \nItaly Large Caliber \nWeapon \n28,22,962 \nTotal  Planned Value of Export in 2016 -17  \n(USD). \n52,73,287  \n \n****** \n\nANNEXURE-I  REFERRED IN THE REPLY GIVEN IN THE STATEMENT  IN \nPART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 347 FOR ANSWER ON \n9.12.2016 \n \n*Value of Turnover for Last Two Years & Current Year   \n(Including Issues to Sister Factories)                          In Rs. Crore  \nSl. \nNo. Factory 2014-15 2015-16 2016-1 7 \n(upto   03/12/2016) \nAmmunition & Explosives (AE) Division \n1 Ammunition Factory, Khadki 896.04 901.48 486.85 \n2 Cordite Factory, Aruvankadu 154.39 185.78 128.47 \n3 High Explosives Factory, Khadki 193.39 231.86 128.69 \n4 Ordnance Factory Khamaria 1410.40 1848.23 473.64 \n5 Ordnance Factory Bhandara 322.93 374.31 171.45 \n6 Ordnance Factory Varangaon 477.48 531.37 164.07 \n7 Ordnance Factory Chanda 1336.61 1529.01 598.43 \n8 Ordnance Factory Bolangir 819.82 911.60 599.71 \n9 Ordnance Factory Itarsi 223.66 274.11 110.94 \n10 Ordnance Factory Dehu Road 294.85 257.67 123.34 \n11 Ordnance Factory Nalanda 0.00 6.02 18.11 \nSub Total : 6,129.57 7,051.44 3,003.70 \nWeapons, Vehicles & Equipment  (WV&E) Division  \n1 Gun Carriage Factory, Jabalpur 513.23 605.08 265.96 \n2 Rifle Factory Ishapore 303.53 295.80 169.81 \n3 Gun & Shell Factory, Cossipore 517.48 599.15 347.38 \n……2/- \n\n \n:  2  : \n \n4 Ordnance Factory Kanpur 561.13 643.07 412.89 \n5 Small Arms Factory, Kanpur 149.27 179.89 94.82 \n6 Ordnance Factory DumDum 130.78 133.19 74.22 \n7 Ordnance Factory Trichy 136.53 101.67 75.80 \n8 Field Gun Factory, Kanpur 242.61 275.53 186.83 \n9 Ordnance Factory Korwa 0.00 7.46 7.09 \n10 Vehicle Factory Jabalpur 1288.28 977.56 665.06 \n11 Grey Iron Foundry Jabalpur 96 150.11 67.98 \nSub Total : 3,938.56 3,968.52 2,367.84 \nMaterials & Components (M&C) Division \n1 Metal & Steel Factory Ishapore 435.09 475.15 311.46 \n2 Ordnance Factory Ambernath 567.00 527.78 312.98 \n3 Ordnance Factory Katni 252.00 284.04 131.74 \n4 Ordnance Factory Muradnagar 203.35 232.73 162.89 \n5 Ordnance Factory Bhusawal 131.94 143.99 114.26 \n6 Machine Prototype Factory, \nAmbernath 164.23 189.11 135.85 \n7 Ordnance Factory Ambajhari 740.47 931.93 549.40 \n8 Heavy Alloy Penetrator Project, \nTrichy 143.86 164.88 96.37 \nSub Total : 2,637.94 2,949.61 1,814.95 \n \n……3/- \n \n \n \n\n \n:  3  : \n \nArmoured Vehicles (AV) Division \n1 Ordnance Cable Factory \nChandigarh 64.13 58.58 40.36 \n2 Ordnance Factory Dehradun 130.17 152.82 162.92 \n3 Heavy Vehicles Factory, Avadi 1118.13 1357.22 1064.26 \n4 Ordnance Factory Medak 697.53 815.87 378.80 \n5 Engine Factory, Avadi 320.35 396.24 328.2 \n6 Opto-Electronics Factory, \nDehradun 222.89 434.97 474.14 \nSub Total : 2,553.20 3,215.70 2,448.68 \nOrdnance Equipment Factories  Division  \n1 Ordnance Equipment Factory \nKanpur  462.39 548.27 383.18 \n2 Ordnance Clothing Factory, \nShajahanpur 441.22 634.15 436.68 \n3 Ordnance Parachute Factory \nKanpur 166.49 234.79 162.77 \n4 Ordnance Clothing Factory Avadi 222.80 300.29 189.06 \n5 Ordnance Equipment Factory \nHajratpur 111.46 150.16 114.99 \nSub Total : 1,404.36 1,867.67 1,286.68 \nGRAND TOTAL * 16,663 * 19,053 *10,921.85 \n*  Value of Turnover is without Excise Duty  \n \n******* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_348": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 348 \nANSWERED ON FRIDAY, THE 09TH DECEMBER, 2016 \n[AGRAHAYANA 18, 1938 (SAKA)] \n \nREGISTRATION OF COMPANIES WITH ROCs \n \nQUESTION \n \n*348.  SHRI GOPAL SHETTY: \n   \nWill the Minister of CORPORATE AFFAIRS                     \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a large number of companies especially in rural areas \nare functioning without being registered with the Registrar of \nCompanies (ROCs) and if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise; \n \n(b) whether it is mandatory for a company to get registered it with \nROCs within a stipulated time period and if so, the details and the \nnorms fixed in this regard; and \n \n(c) the action taken by the Government against erring companies \nduring the last three years and the current year, Year/ State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS              (SHRI ARUN JAITLEY) \n \n (a) to (c) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF THE \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 348 FOR ANSWER IN LOK SABHA \nON 09-12-2016 \n(a) & (c): The Ministry has received seven complaints during the last \nthree years and current year (up to 30 -11-2016) in respect of \ncompanies allegedly carrying out operations without getting \nregistered under the Companies Act. The details of complaints and \naction taken thereupon by the respective Registrars of Companies \nare enclosed as Annexure-I. \n(b)  Yes, it is mandatory to get a company registered for conducting \nbusiness as an entity incorporated under the Companies Act. The \nincorporation of a company is done by following the provisions \nprescribed under Chapter II of the Companies Act, 2013 read with the \nCompanies (Registration Offices and Fees) Rules, 2014 framed \nthereunder and amendments thereto from time to time.  Further, \nsection 453 of the Companies Act, 2013 prescribes punishment for \nimproper use of word “Limited” or words “Private Limited”. \n****** \n  \n\nAnnexure - I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (c) OF THE STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 348 FOR ANSWER IN LOK SABHA ON 09.12.2016 \n \nDetails of companies against whom complaints received for operating \nwithout incorporation \nS. \nNo. \nName of the \nCompany \nRegistrar of \nCompanies \nAction Taken \n1. Webtern India \nPrivate Limited \nROC, Pune Matter referred to Economic Offences \nWing as no such company was found at \nthe address provided by the complainant \n2. Tanishka \nInfotech Private \nLimited \nROC, Pune Matter referred to Economic Offences \nWing as no such company was found at \nthe address provided by the \ncomplainant. \n3. Corporate \nSolutions and \nHospitality \nServices Private \nLimited \nROC, \nBangalore \nThe complaint wa s closed as no such \ncompany was found at the address \nprovided by the complainant and there \nwas no response to the reference made \nto the complainant to provide further \ndetails. \n4. Krishi Vipran \nVikas Limited \nROC, \nKanpur \nThe complaint was examined and it was \nobserved that the company was \nfunctioning without incorporation under \nthe Companies Act. The ROC has filed \nprosecution under section 453 of the \nCompanies Act, 2013 for the default. \n5. Speakasia \nOnline Pte. \nLimited (an \nunregistered \nforeign \ncompany) \nROC, Delhi Serious Fraud Investigation Office \n(SFIO) of this Ministry has conducted \ninvestigation of the said company and \nhas filed prosecution under various \nprovisions of the Companies Act, 1956 \nas well as under the Indian Penal Code \nfor the offences reported. \n6. Bhagya Laxmi \nFinance Private \nLimited \nROC, Delhi The complaint has been referred to the \nDepartment of Electronics & \nInformation Technology (the entity was \nrunning a website in this name) as the \nletter issued to the company by ROC, \nDelhi office was received back \nundelivered. \n7. Natraj Finance ROC, Delhi The complaint has been examined and a \nreport submitted by ROC, Delhi in the \n\nmatter is under examination in the \nMinistry. \n \n****** ",
