    "ls|LS16_S10_U_389": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.389 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2016 \n \nRASHTRIYA RAIL SANRAKSHA KOSH \n \n*389.  SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT: \n SHRI B. SRIRAMULU:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has proposed creation of the Rashtriya Rail \nSanrakha Kosh (RRSK) with a view to give additional emphasis on the \nsafety and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Ministry of Finance has given its approval for the creation of \nthe said kosh; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and further action taken by the Government in \nthis regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 389 BY SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT & SHRI B. SRIRAMULU TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 14.12.2016 REGARDING RASHTRIYA RAIL \nSANRAKSHA KOSH \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. Ministry of Railways has proposed to create a non-lapsible \n“Rastriya Rail Sanraksha Kosh” (RRSK) totaling ì 1,19,183 Crores, out of \nwhich ì 1,11,683 Crores to be funded by Ministry of Finance for safety \nimprovement of Indian Railways. The safety related works identified \nwith approximate fund requirement are as under:   \nSN Item Approx. Fund  \n(ì  in Cr.) \n1.  Track Works 30032 \n2.  Bridge Rehabilitation Works 3250 \n3.  Other safety works for Track Vehicular \nUltrasonic testing system for Rail/Welds etc. \n11697 \n4.  Safety Works at Level Crossing (Elimination of \nLC, ROB/RUB/Subway etc.) \n43444 \n5.  S&T replacement and improvement works 10140 \n6.  Rolling Stock replacement and improvement \nworks \n9263.55 \n7.  OHE replacement and other electrical \nimprovement work \n9495 \n8.  Human Resource Development 1861.45 \n Grand Total 1,19,183 \n \n \n-2- \n\n(b) & (c) Hon’ble Finance Minister has agreed to constitute the fund subject \nto conditions that 75% of the total requirement should be financed  by \nMinistry of Railways through resource mobilization and balance 25% of the \nrequirement will be provided out of the Gross Budgetary Support (GBS) \nmade available by General Revenues over a period of 5 years. The matter is \nbeing pursued with Ministry of Finance.  \n \n***** \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_390": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 390 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \nSHORTAGE OF OFFICIALS IN PANCHAYATS \n \n†390 SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \n  \n Will the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n \n(a) Whether there is shortage of officers/employees at Panchayat, Block Samiti and Zila \nParishad level in States including Uttar Pradesh; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/ UT-wise; \n(c) whether there is shortage of basic infrastructure like office, compute risation of \nPanchayats and training of various representatives/ officers of Panchayati Raj to meet the \nneeds of all Gram Panchayats; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the amount allocated and utilised during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \n \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA) \n \n(a) to (d) Yes , Madam. As per the information received from State s/UTs, there is a \nshortage of staff, basic infrastructure viz office buildings and computers at each level of \nPanchayats; and there exist gaps in the capacities of elected representatives and functionaries \nof Panchayats in most of the States/UTs including Uttar Pradesh to be able to discharge their \nfunctions properly. ‘Panchayat’ being a State subject, the primary responsibility for providing \nsuch facilities vest s with the States. The details of officers/employees and infrastructure in \nPanchayats are not maintained by the Ministry of Panchayati Raj. \n \nThe Ministry of Panchayati Raj has been augmenting the efforts of the States under \nthe Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan [erstwhile Rajiv Gandhi Panchayat Sashaktikaran \nAbhiyan (RGPSA)] scheme. The financial and technical support has been provided to States \nfor strengthening Panchayats including for administrative and technical support, co nstruction \nand maintenance of Gram Panchayat buildings, computers and training and  capacity building \nof various stakeholders of Panchayats. With effect from the financial year 2015-16, the \nsupport for administrative and technical items, construction and maintenance of Gram \nPanchayat buildings, and computers has been discontinued.  \n  \nThe funds were also provided under district component of the Backward Regions \nGrant Fund Programme (BRGF) for supplementing and converging existing developmental \ninflows into identified backward districts so as to bridge critical gaps in local infrastructure \nand other development requirements. With effect from the financial year 2015 -16, the BRGF \nhas been delinked from the budgetary support of the Central Government. \n \nThe details of funds released and utilised by States/ UTs are given at Annexe I and II. \n \n**** \n \n\n \nAnnexe I \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Part (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha unstarred Question No -390 regarding \nShortage of Officials in Panchayats to be answered on 17.11.2016. \n \nStatus regarding State -wise Funds Released & Funds utilized under RGPSA/RGSA during 2013 -14 to \n2016-17 \n            (Rs. in crores) \nS.No. Name of the \nState/ UTs \n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \nFunds \nRelease\nd  \nFunds \nUtilized*    \nFunds \nReleased  \nFunds \nUtilized*  \nFunds \nReleased                       \nFunds \nUtilized*   \nFunds \nRelease\nd                       \nFunds \nUtilized \n* * \n1 Assam 16.65 16.65 26.04 26.04 17.08 11.66 21.83   \n2 Andhra \nPradesh 41.6 41.6 24.19 24.19 12.5 10.6 45.8   \n3 Arunachal \nPradesh 8.71 8.71 7.72 7.28 0       \n4 Bihar 8.61 0 63.67 0 0       \n5 Chhattisgarh 25.73 25.73 11.4 11.4 14.64 10.72 21.31   \n6 Gujarat 31.65 31.65 1.06 1.06 0   33.38   \n7 Haryana 2.93 2.93 18.78 6.25 0       \n8 Himachal \nPradesh 15.84 15.84 15.26 7.78 2.48       \n9 Jammu & \nKashmir 9.45 0 8.58 0 0       \n10 Jharkhand 16.45 15.83 16.2 14.36 9.49   20.9   \n11 Karnataka 25.56 25.56 46.8 46.74 32.71 0     \n12 Kerala 16.58 16.58 14.49 11.28 0   8.55