    "ls|LS16_S10_U_448": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER & SANITATION \n \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 448 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \nPiped Water Supply to Rural Habitations \n \n448.  SHRIMATI P.K. SREEMATHI TEACHER \n  SHRI MALLIKARJUN  KHARGE \n  SHRI JANAK  RAM \nSHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY \nSHRI HARI MANJHI \nDR. VIRENDRA KUMAR: \n  \n \n Will   the Minister   of DRINKING WATER AND SANITAT ION be pleased to \nstate? \n(a)   the number of rural households and habitation s along with their percentage covered \nunder Piped Water Supply(PWS) in the country, State-wise; \n(b)  the details of the funds allocated, released a nd utilised for PWS during each of the \nlast three years and the current year indicating the funds likely to be spent to achieve \nthe targets fixed in this regard, State-wise; \n(c)  the steps taken by the Government to provide P WS to all the rural habitations; \n(d)  whether the Government has undertaken review o f the PWS in all the States and if \nso, the details of the outcome thereof, State-wise; and \n(e)  whether the Government has fixed any time-fram e to provide PWS to all the rural \npopulation in the country and if so, the details th ereof and the steps being taken in \npursuance thereof, State/UT-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE INTHE MINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER  SANITATION \n(SHRI RAMESH CHANDAPPA JIGAJINAGI) \n \n \na) State-wise details of number of Rural Households an d Habitations along with their \npercentage covered under Piped Water Supply(PWS) in  the country; are at \nAnnexure-‘I’ . \n \nb) Under NRDWP funds are released to the States to sup plement their efforts to \nprovide drinking water to the rural population in t he country. Though the Ministry \n\nencourages coverage of habitations with piped water  supply it is for the States to \ndecide with regard to the type of schemes to be und ertaken.   State-wise details of \nfunds allocated, released and utilized under NRDWP during the last three years and \nthe current financial year are at Annexure-‘II’. \n \nc) This Ministry has made a Strategic Plan for providi ng drinking water supply in rural \nareas of the Country. The emphasis is on providing drinking water supply through \npiped water supply.  Under the Strategic Plan for r ural drinking water supply for the \nperiod 2011-2022, the interim goal till 2017 is to cover 50% of all rural households \nwith piped water supply. By 2022, the goal is to co ver 90% of rural households with \npiped water supply. \n \nd) Drinking water supply is a State subject. Governmen t of India supplements the \nefforts of the State Governments with technical and  financial assistance for \nprovision of safe drinking water supply in the rura l areas of the country under the \ncentrally sponsored National Rural Drinking Water P rogramme (NRDWP). The \nState Governments are vested with powers to select,  plan, approve and implement \ndrinking water supply schemes under the NRDWP, to c over more or left out \nhabitations with piped drinking water supply. The M inistry encourages the coverage \nof habitations with piped water supply and at prese nt 52.95 percent of the rural \npopulation is covered with piped water supply eithe r through stand post or through \nhousehold tap connection.   \n \ne) As per this Ministry’s Strategic Plan, the goal is to cover 90% of rural households \nwith piped water supply. On 9/10.09.2016, a Nationa l workshop with the states was \nheld followed by series of meeting to review the ex isting scenario of coverage of \nPiped Water Supply vis-à-vis the States strategy to  achieve full coverage of Piped \nWater Supply to all habitations in rural areas as p er Strategic Plan of this Ministry \nand the total requirement of funds to achieve the g oal. The States were directed to \nupgrade ground water based schemes into surface wat er based schemes and to \nintegrate existing system like reservoirs / trunk m ain / distribution pipe lines in \nsurface based group water supply schemes, wherever possible. \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I\nAnnexure referred to in part (a) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Q. No. 448 for 17.11.2016  \nS.No. State/ UTs \nNo. of \nHabitations \ncovered by \nPWS as on \n10/11/2016 \n \n% of Habitations \ncovered by PWS \nas on 10/11/2016 \n \n% of Population \ncovered with \nPWS as on \n10/11/2016 \n% of Household \nconnections with \nPWS as on \n10/11/2016 \nTotal \nHousehold \nconnections \nas on \n(10/11/2016) \n \n1 Andaman And Nicobar  254  63.5  91.36  10.15  6604  \n2 Andhra Pradesh  38496  79.63  95.15  21.43  1956240  \n3 Arunachal Pradesh  3571  47.13  59.53  4.37  9729  \n4 Assam  33477  38  44.61  1.88  109042  \n5 Bihar  6719  6.09  10.58  0.58  103705  \n6 Chandigarh  0 0 0 0 0 \n7 Chattisgarh  16230  21.75  37.28  6.67  288143  \n8 Dadra & Nagar Haveli  0 0 0 0 0 \n9 Daman & Diu  0 0 0 0 0 \n10  Goa  0 0 0 0 0 \n11  Gujarat  32120  89.06  94.54  69.8  4521179  \n12  Haryana  7701  96.89  98.8  41.11  1358689  \n13  Himachal Pradesh  52276  97.52  96.06  54.3  728681  \n14  Jammu And Kashmir  14937  93.6  94.18  27.76  458046  \n15  Jharkhand  12362  10.29  20.41  2.98  148240  \n16  Karnataka  52222  86.72  99.6  36.92  3021171  \n17  Kerala  11999  100.97  100 .00  13.6  781502  \n18  Lakshadweep  0 0 0 0 0 \n19  Madhya Pradesh  21167  16.53  37.87  7.97  869388  \n20  Maharashtra  67970  67.92  83.35  35.41  4759490  \n21  Manipur  2686  93.65  96.43  3.64  15885  \n22  Meghalaya  6037  57.63  66.78  0.7  3301  \n23  Mizoram  667  90.38  93.86  11.17  11705  \n24  Nagaland  1474  96.34  100 .00  4.88  16144  \n25  Odisha  37170  23.76  41.86  2.15  174517  \n26  Puducherry  118  44.36  55.36  49.06  40358  \n27  Punjab  13065  84.92  91.6  39.69  1333376  \n28  Rajasthan  41897  34.44  51.79  10.83  1007658  \n29  Sikkim  2082  99.91  99.93  77.81  69004  \n30  Tamil Nadu  99484  99.28  99.54  26.96  2662339  \n31  Telangana  22161  90.15  98.82  31.91  1758031  \n32  Tripura  6103  6