    "ls|LS16_S10_U_453": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 453 \nANSWERED ON 17TH NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nPROJECTS UNDER CENTRAL ROAD FUND \n \n453.  SHRIMATI RAMA DEVI: \nSHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \nSHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM: \nSHRI ANOOP MISHRA: \n \n             Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसडक परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) the criteria being adopted for allocation of funds to States for development of State roads under Central Road \nFund (CRF) scheme; \n(b) the details of the proposals received and approved under the said scheme during the last three years and the \ncurrent year, State-wise; \n(c) the details of the CRF accruals and releases under the scheme during the said period, State-wise; \n(d) the details of the pending and rejected proposals, State -wise along with the reasons therefor and the time by \nwhich the remaining proposals are likely to be cleared; \n(e) the details of the places where construction works have been undertaken under CRF d uring the said period, \nState and year-wise; and \n(f) whether  any over -bridges are being constructed with central assistance in the country, if so, the details \nthereof State-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n \n(SHRI PON. RADHAKRISHNAN) \n \n (a) Ministry allocates funds to the States/Union Territories  (UTs) for development of State Roads  (Non-\nRural Roads) under the CRF scheme. The funds for development of State roads under CRF scheme are allocated \nto the States/UTs on the basis of 30 percent weightage to fuel consumption and 70 percent weightage to the \ngeographical area. The fund under CRF is non -lapsable. Apart from this, the Ministry also allocates funds for \ndevelopment of State Roads of Economic Importance and Inter -State Connectivity (EI & ISC) as per the CRF \nAct,2000 amended by the Finance Act from time to time.   \n \n(b) to (d) The identification, prioritization and selection of projects for approval/ sanction under CRF and \nEI&ISC schemes are governed by CRF (State Roads) Rules, 2014 amen ded by CRF (State Roads) A mendment \nRules, 2016. Further, the limits of total approval of projects out of the proposal received from the concerned \nState Government in a particular year is also governed by the said Rules.   \n \nThe State/ Union Territories (UTs) -wise details of projects approved / sanctioned for development of \nState Roads under CRF and EI & ISC Schemes during the last three years and current year are at Annexure -I & \nAnnexure-II respectively.  \nState/ UT-wise details of accrual/allocation and expen diture/release of funds under CRF and EI & ISC \nSchemes during the last three years and current year are at Annexure-III.  \n \n(e) and (f)  The information is being compiled and the same shall be laid on the table of the house. \n \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART S (b) to (d) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 435 FOR ANSWER ON 17.11.2016  ASKED BY SHRIMATI \nRAMA DEVI AND OTHERS REGARDING PROJECTS UNDER CENTRAL ROAD FUND \n \n \nThe State / UT-wise details of projects approved / sanctioned for development of State Roads \nunder CRF during the last three years and current year \n(Amount in Rs. crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState/UT \n  \n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17* \nNos. Cost Nos. Cost Nos. Cost Nos. Cost \n  States  \n1. Andhra Pradesh 55 584.25 - - 1 5.50 61 619.00 \n2. Arunachal Pradesh - - 8 97.94 9 80.74 - - \n3. Assam 9 61.87 9 90.03 16 66.84 - - \n4. Bihar 5 205.74 9 124.67 - - - - \n5. Chhattisgarh - - 10 305.56 - - - - \n6. Goa 5 58.82 1 29.42 - - - - \n7. Gujarat 14 95.20 - - 9 473.02 - - \n8. Haryana 4 99.53 - - 11 280.91 15 366.05 \n9. Himachal Pradesh 6 48.93 14 55.59 44 197.01 - - \n10. Jammu & Kashmir 8 110.67 17 347.41 25 785.56 - - \n11. Jharkhand 2 98.21 2 16.25 5 252.71 - - \n12. Karnataka 256 1,000.00 15 70.50 - 