    "ls|LS16_S10_U_487": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 487\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016\nESTABLISHMENT OF PHYSIOTHERAPY COUNCIL\n487. DR. GOKARAJU GANGA RAJU:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government proposes to establish Physiotherapy Council on the line of Medical\nCouncil of India (MCI) in order to check the quality of education in the stream;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor and the other measures/steps taken by the Government to address\nthe problem of low intake of students opting to be physiotherapists?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI FAGGAN SINGH KULASTE)\n(a): No.\n(b): Does not arise.\n(c): Physiotherapy is a part of Allied Health and a separate Council for each discipline under\nthe broad umbrella of Allied Health is not required.",
    "ls|LS16_S10_U_488": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF FINANCE\nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 488\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016 / 27 KARTIKA, 1938 (SAKA)\nBANKING OMBUDSMAN\nQUESTION\n488. SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL:\n            \n Will the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of complaints/grievances received, settled and pending by Banking Ombudsman during the last three years and the current year, \npublic and private bank-wise, State-wise;\n(b) the number of Banking Ombudsman officers appointed over the last three years and the current year;\n(c) whether the staff strength in the Banking Ombudsman is inadequate for handling the increasing number of complaints; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken by the Government to improve working condition and settle the pending cases expeditiously?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE\n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR)\n (a): The information relating to number of complaints / grievances received, settled and pending (bank-wise) in Banking Ombudsman offices during \nlast three years i.e. 2013-14, 2014-15, and 2015-16 and current year relating to public and private sector banks, is given  at Annexure.  The state-\nwise information is not maintained with the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).\n\n(b) to (d): There are 16 offices of Banking Ombudsman in the country.   The total staff strength of the Offices of the Banking Ombudsman and the \nnumber of complaints received during last three years is given below.  The staff position undergoes change on account of transfer/retirements of the \nofficials.  With the existing staff strength, the Offices of Banking Ombudsman achieved a disposal rate of above 95% during the last three years.  \nThe details are as under:-\nYear 2013-2014 2014-2015 2015-2016\nNo. of complaints \nreceived\n76573 85131 102894\nNo. of officers 167 149 141\n*****\n\nAnnexure referred to in reply to Par